WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.120
-Trudeau denies the report, Ed.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.040
Sounds like a rough week for Canada's first black Prime Minister, thanks Tim.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.520
A problem long posed, now finally an answer

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.840
a cure has been found to a rare form of cancer.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.040
We'll tell you found it, what he thinks this means

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.500
and dig up some tweets from his early teens.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.720
Plus the good samaritan whose quickness and breadth

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.300
saved a family of four from a fiery death.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.460
We'll ask how he did it, how me made it in time,

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.940
and why he tweeted this in 2009.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.180
Uh Ed? Yes Tim?

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.260
Forgive the defiance,

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.760
but I think we should focus on the news part, the science,

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.060
and not what they tweeted back when they were ten.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.280
The science, hmm, I'll try it again.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.880
Archeologists have unearthed a series of tweets

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.120
made by this local hero when he was 13.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.600
Will this middle school tweet mean his demise?

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.080
Our report just might win a Pulitzer prize.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.240
A Pulitzer prize in what? Scrolling down?

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.760
We found immature things immature people wrote down.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.220
Our country's at war and that's the story we sought.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.220
War coverage, yes, I'll give it a shot.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.900
This Navy SEAL unit is now under fire for a series of tweets,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.540
we'll take our magnifier and pay no attention to how their recent life's been

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.920
tell you what you should think that says about them.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.020
Says about them? What's it say about us?

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.620
That the first thing we do after someone's discussed

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.020
Is comb through their childhood looking for dirt.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.280
OK, I can do this, I assure you I'm cured.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.640
Well she's the first woman to serve on the board

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.940
Of our town's city council—and she just signed an accord.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.300
We'll comb through the details of what she did write

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.560
And through years of her tweets in hopes of wrecking her life.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.040
OK, see, I hate this, this is just what we do

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.440
Make things controversial for clicks and for views.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.900
When we're covering news, should our first thought each time

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.160
Be "Let's find what they tweeted back when they were nine"?

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.680
Finally, millions can now walk thanks to his prosthesis

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.960
But a hateful hand signal when he was a fetus

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.180
Leads many to now question what he promotes.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.920
We'll toss him in a well and see if he floats.

